Author:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Nov 5 11:46:53 2026 -0500
Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Nov 5 11:46:53 2026 -0500

    fix(http): key the rate-limit bucket on the principal, not the peer IP (HARDEN-DUCKBRAIN-003 B)
    
    Every fleet caller on this host shares 127.0.0.1, so the per-IP token bucket
    collapsed them into one budget: one agent's burst returned 429 to every other
    agent's requests. The limiter now spends from `principal:<sha256(key)>` when the
    live credential snapshot knows the presented x-api-key (constant-time match,
    cached snapshot), and from `ip:<peer>` for anonymous / unrecognized / basic-auth
    callers — so guessing a key mints no fresh budget and credential stuffing stays
    bounded by address. Store size is capped with oldest-bucket eviction.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
